  w6_title: 'Find the box', w6_body: 'Box and this device must be on the SAME Wi‑Fi.', w6_bodyUsb: 'Connect the box to this computer with a DATA USB cable.', w6_scan: 'Scanning the network…', w6_scanUsb: 'Looking for a box on USB…', w6_found: 'Found', w6_manual: 'Or enter manually', w6_ip: 'IP address', w6_pair: 'Pairing code', w6_port: 'Port', w6_none: 'Nothing found', w6_rescan: 'Scan again', w6_pick: 'Choose the box', w6_pickD: 'Chrome asks which device this page may use.', w6_pickNone: 'Chrome had nothing to offer, or the dialog was closed. Most TV boxes have USB ports for sticks and keyboards only — the ones that work this way have a DATA port (micro‑USB or USB‑C, often marked OTG). If yours has none, go back and use network debugging over Wi‑Fi.', w6_pickNoAdb: 'That device is plugged in, but nothing on it speaks ADB. Check that USB debugging is on, and that the cable is in the box’s DATA port — not the one for sticks.',
  w6_ts1: 'Same router? On the box, Settings › Network shows its IP. It has to start like this computer’s — a box on another router (or its guest Wi‑Fi) cannot be reached at all.', w6_ts2: 'USB plugged but nothing listed? Install the USB driver (Windows).', w6_ts3: 'Found it once and now nothing? Many boxes drop Network debugging after a reboot or standby — check the switch on the box, then scan again.', w6_u1: 'Is it the port you plug a mouse into? That one is the box DRIVING a device. ADB needs the box to BE the device — a micro‑USB or USB‑C port, often marked OTG.', w6_u2: 'Is it a data cable? Charging cables have no data wires, and Windows lists nothing at all.', w6_u3: 'Still nothing? Most TV boxes have no device port — network debugging over Wi‑Fi is the way in.', w6_hotspot: 'Hotspot guide', w6_driver: 'Get USB driver',
